'' A bare '= value' over a UDT field with a converting constructor runs that constructor
'' ON THE FIELD, in place of the default one. It declined into the aggregate SkipHere, so
'' 'TwsHost as DWSTRING = "127.0.0.1"' was default-constructed and left empty and tracks
'' could not connect to TWS. Measured, fbc-modern prints 'shared [default] 7496
'' [s:127.0.0.1:0]', 'local [s:127.0.0.1:0]', 'new [s:127.0.0.1:0]' and 'default
'' constructors: 3' -- the same lines tiko-lang now prints.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/field-init-convctor.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' The argument is a REAL descriptor, assigned, passed and deleted -- fbc's shape. A pool
'' descriptor from fb_StrAllocTempDescZEx is never released by a user constructor, and
'' tracks' grid built enough of them to drain the pool: every later temporary string
'' came back empty.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrAssign(@$tmp0, -1, @@$str13, 10, 0)
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN1WC1ER8FBSTRINGj(%5, @$tmp0, %12)
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl void fb_StrDelete(@$tmp0)
'' ...and NOT the default constructor before it: 'plain' at offset 0 gets one, 'host'
'' does not.
'' EXPECT-NOT: call void _ZN1WC1Ev(%5)
